; The project path contains "&" (Document Intelligence & RAG Platform),
; which cmd.exe (npm's default Windows script-shell) misparses as a
; command separator, corrupting node_modules/.bin shim paths. Use Git
; Bash instead, which handles the "&" in the path correctly.
;
; Must be Git\bin\bash.exe, not Git\usr\bin\bash.exe: the usr\bin copy is
; the raw MSYS2 bash and doesn't set up its own PATH when invoked
; non-interactively (as npm does), so it can't find sed/dirname/uname
; even though they sit right next to it. Git\bin\bash.exe sets up that
; environment before running, so npm's generated shell shims work.
script-shell="C:\\Program Files\\Git\\bin\\bash.exe"
